Z||000003||artherd||09-02-2001||08:33 PM||||Shift cables from a "cross", and the end cap (hard to get to) is feromagnetic.<P>It also looks evil  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (and has a slightly crappy casting in my expierence, just look duller than the metal used for the isuzus for instance.)  That's all the ways I know of, heh.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by beachbomb:<BR><B>Whats the easiest way to recongnize a getrag transmission?..thanks..jim(2 '84 Indys)<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigzach_28.JPG">  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||rockcrawl||09-02-2001||09:33 PM||||Take a magnet. The Getrag is the only one with a steel end plate. If a magnet sticks to it it's a getrag.||||reg||1
Z||000005||LS1swap||09-02-2001||10:18 PM||||Shift cables- one under one over. Cover on back of transmission ferrous metal (magnetic) has nine bolts not seven. Here are some pics. Note in the second pic you can see the top shift cable the other one comes from undernieth<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/25_22.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/19_16.jpg"> ||||reg||1
